    "https://careers.ucalgary.ca/": {
      "title": "UCalgary Careers",
      "description": "University of Calgary Careers Skip to main content Menu Careers Home See All Jobs Candidate Information Total Rewards at UCalgary Workplace Diversity and Inclusion Indigenous Candidates Accessibility and Accommodation Application FAQ's UCalgary Careers Search by keyword All Types Academic Management and Staff Postdoc FA1 FA2 FA3 FA4 FA5 FA6 FA7 FA8 FA9 VRS SAG ASA FIN HRL HRS INT LBS MGT PRO RSS SKT SLT STU TEC PDF All Faculties/Units Administrative Offices and Institutes Continuing Education Cumming School of Medicine Facilities Faculty of Arts Faculty of Graduate Studies Faculty of Kinesiology Faculty of Law Faculty of Nursing Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Work Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Finance, HR, IT, and Services Haskayne School of Business Libraries and Cultural Resources Office of Development and Alumni Office of External Relations School of Architecture, Planning and Landscape Schulich School of Engineering Student Enrolment Services Werklund School of Education 54210 54025 80025 54365 54510 68010 80010 80040 80510 80550 80590 80131 54550 65002 80560 80670 38010 28011 62010 62055 80035 62157 62151 15010 22010 32500 25010 29010 12010 33500 30000 65000 66000 80030 80031 67010 60010 68025 68035 80037 80065 80045 14101 54140 81010 81510 81080 37500 20010 54270 54315 18010 Current employee? View the Internal Careers website . Be part of an ambitious university At the University of Calgary, we don’t wait for change. We make change. A new solution for a problem, a new creative composition, a new look for a downtown block or a new technology to transform the marketplace – we’re here to help Calgary’s economy, grow, prosper, and diversify in the years ahead. UCalgary is where people come to Start something . UCalgary has been recognized as one of Canada’s top research universities. The future of UCalgary and our city is connected, and is at the heart of why we continually work to build meaningful relationships that support our community and economy. Through partnering with businesses, social groups and governments we are adding value – and you can too. Note: Be familiar with UCalgary's recruitment standards Cybercriminals may attempt to recreate UCalgary's website or print materials in an attempt to legitimize their fraudulent activities. Learn more about Recruitment Fraud here https://www.calgaryeconomicdevelopment.com/live-and-work/ Work in a leading city Learn more https://www.ucalgary.ca/news/ucalgary-research Work where it makes a difference Learn more https://www.ucalgary.ca/hr/campus-culture/diversity-careers Work where you belong Learn more /pages/academic-careers Academic Careers Learn more /pages/management-and-staff-careers Management & Staff Careers Learn more /pages/postdoc-careers Postdoc Opportunities Learn more UCalgary – A Great Place to Work Alberta’s Top Employers is a special designation recognizing Alberta employers that lead their industries in offering exceptional places to work. Canada’s Best Diversity Employers recognizes organizations from across Canada with exceptional workplace diversity and inclusiveness programs. What Makes Working at UCalgary Great? Start something Self-discovery starts at UCalgary. Focus your potential through innovative learning experiences, bold discoveries and lifelong connections. Find your starting line. Learn more Benefits We have comprehensive benefit programs, a variety of learning opportunities and an inclusive Employee and Family Assistance Program that offers a wide variety of immediate and confidential support to employees and their family. Learn more Drive your career Part of the university working experience includes access to a mix of professional and personal learning and growth opportunities. This includes access to our Tuition Support program . Belonging UCalgary is committed to pluralism, and to an equitable, diverse, inclusive and accessible campus. We are dedicated to creating safe environments for all, including gender-diverse, culturally diverse and intersex members of our campus community. Events like EDI Week and resources through the Faith and Spirituality Centre , the Writing Symbols Lodge , Student Accessibility Services , the Q Centre , and the Women's Resource Centre contribute to a campus that is full of different ideas and spaces for everyone. Flourish At UCalgary we understand the importance of our campus community’s mental health and well-being and have a bold strategy to create a community of caring. We offer hybrid work options and flextime so that you can feel and do your best. We offer programs and services that promote healthy living, a healthy work environment, and a healthy life outside of work. Learn more about wellbeing & worklife balance and our benefits and pension plan . Vibrant Campus Our main campus enjoys beautiful and ethical green spaces, trees and ponds that build resiliency and adaptation while respecting natural laws and focuses on community well-being. There is also easy access to the trendy University District. Our other campuses, located both near (e.g. Downtown campus) and far (e.g. Doha, Qatar), offer a number of amenities and great surroundings for employees to enjoy. Learn more UCalgary and The Office of Institutional Commitments (OIC) are committed to a equitable, diverse, and inclusive campus that is accessible to all and free from harassment, bullying, and discrimination. We strive to remove barriers faced by equity-deserving groups, including women, Indigenous peoples, visible/racialized minorities, persons with disabilities, and LGBTQ2S+. The OIC provides resources and education to foster a community of change-makers, promoting workplace diversity and inclusion as core values essential to campus well-being. Search All Opportunities Now Opportunities with an Indigenous Scope or Focus The Office of Indigenous Engagement and ii' taa'poh'to'p guide UCalgary on its path of transformation,and communicate its commitment and responsibility for truth and reconciliation. We are embracing new ways of knowing, ways of doing, ways of connecting and ways of being. We are exploring our past, incorporating Indigenous knowledge into our research and practices and breaking down barriers to access education . We are committed to doing things differently where we are walking on a parallel path with Indigenous peoples in a shared, ethical way. Search Opportunities Ready to take the next step? Apply today facebook twitter linkedin instagram youtube Digital Privacy Statement Privacy Policy Website Feedback University of Calgary 2500 University Drive NW Calgary Alberta T2N 1N4 CANADA Copyright © 2026 The University of Calgary, located in the heart of Southern Alberta, both acknowledges and pays tribute to the traditional territories of the peoples of Treaty 7, which include the Blackfoot Confederacy (comprised of the Siksika, the Piikani, and the Kainai First Nations), the Tsuut’ina First Nation, and the Stoney Nakoda (including Chiniki, Bearspaw, and Goodstoney First Nations). The City of Calgary is also home to Métis Nation within Alberta (Nose Hill Métis District 5 and Elbow Métis District 6). The University of Calgary is situated on land Northwest of where the Bow River meets the Elbow River, a site traditionally known as Moh’kins’tsis to the Blackfoot, Wîchîspa to the Stoney Nakoda, and Guts’ists’i to the Tsuut’ina. On this land and in this place we strive to learn together, walk together, and grow together \"in a good way.\" Important Notice Thank you for your interest in viewing our Internal Careers website. Please note the following: You must be a current, active employee in order to use this site You must have your Employee ID number in order to submit your application You must use your Last Name as it appears in the HR system or you will cause an error and delay in your application To confirm your Employee ID and/or the spelling of your Last Name (including use of hyphens (-), apostrophes (‘), etc.), refer to your University ID card or your pay statement available in the myUofC portal (click All about me > My pay > My paycheque ). If you need to update your name in the HR system, you can do so via the portal (click All about me > My info > Name change ). To continue on to the Internal Careers website, click the Continue button below. Exit Continue"
    },
