oximately 6 months.The Calgary... Learn More Medical Office Assistant, Student Wellness Services Job ID: 38471 Location: Main Campus Updated September 01, 2026 Description  Student Wellness Services in Student Experience and Support is currently seeking a Full-time Regular Medical Office Assistant.Student Wellness Services supports and empowers students to... Learn More Schulich Studio Technician, Schulich School of Engineering Job ID: 38468 Location: Main Campus Updated August 31, 2026 Description  SSE Operations Staff in the Schulich School of Engineering is currently seeking a Full-time Limited Term Schulich Studio Technician for approximately 8 months.This position reports to... Learn More Employer Specialist, Engineering Career Centre Job ID: 38467 Location: Main Campus Updated August 31, 2026 Description  The Engineering Career Centre in the Schulich School of Engineering is currently seeking a Full-time Limited Term Employer Specialist for approximately 24 months. Reports to the... Learn More Intermediate Anatomy and Pathology Technician, Faculty of Veterinary Medicine Job ID: 38454 Location: Foothills Campus Updated August 31, 2026 Description  The Faculty of Veterinary Medicine is currently seeking a Full-time Temporary Relief Intermediate Anatomy and Pathology Technician for approximately 1 year.The Intermediate Anatomy and... Learn More Research Assistant (Graduate Student) Job ID: 38441 Location: Main Campus Updated August 28, 2026 Description  The Department of Earth, Energy and Environment in the Faculty of Science invites applications for a Graduate Student Research Assistant - Research - EEE. This part-time position is for... Learn More View more jobs previous 1 2 3 4 5 next Application FAQs facebook twitter linkedin instagram youtube Digital Privacy Statement Privacy Policy Website Feedback University of Calgary 2500 University Drive NW Calgary Alberta T2N 1N4 CANADA Copyright © 2026 The University of Calgary, located in the heart of Southern Alberta, both acknowledges and pays tribute to the traditional territories of the peoples of Treaty 7, which include the Blackfoot Confederacy (comprised of the Siksika, the Piikani, and the Kainai First Nations), the Tsuut’ina First Nation, and the Stoney Nakoda (including Chiniki, Bearspaw, and Goodstoney First Nations). The City of Calgary is also home to Métis Nation within Alberta (Nose Hill Métis District 5 and Elbow Métis District 6). The University of Calgary is situated on land Northwest of where the Bow River meets the Elbow River, a site traditionally known as Moh’kins’tsis to the Blackfoot, Wîchîspa to the Stoney Nakoda, and Guts’ists’i to the Tsuut’ina. On this land and in this place we strive to learn together, walk together, and grow together \"in a good way.\" Important Notice Thank you for your interest in viewing our Internal Careers website. Please note the following: You must be a current, active employee in order to use this site You must have your Employee ID number in order to submit your application You must use your Last Name as it appears in the HR system or you will cause an error and delay in your application To confirm your Employee ID and/or the spelling of your Last Name (including use of hyphens (-), apostrophes (‘), etc.), refer to your University ID card or your pay statement available in the myUofC portal (click All about me > My pay > My paycheque ). If you need to update your name in the HR system, you can do so via the portal (click All about me > My info > Name change ). To continue on to the Internal Careers website, click the Continue button below. Exit Continue"
